{"term":"adjacent","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5703242896099cffb8","definition":"Lying next to, close, or contiguous; neighboring; bordering on.","example":"Because the conference room is filled, we will have our meeting in the adjacent room.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["abutting","adjoining","contiguous","juxtaposed","near","conterminous"],"antonyms":["apart","distant","nonadjacent"],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["adjacency","adjacent angle","adjacently","adjacentness","circumadjacent","coadjacent","comic-adjacent","fetish-adjacent","nonadjacent","subadjacent","unadjacent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjacent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9d9dda005a61568a71","definition":"Just before, after, or facing.","example":"The picture is on the adjacent page.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["adjacency","adjacent angle","adjacently","adjacentness","circumadjacent","coadjacent","comic-adjacent","fetish-adjacent","nonadjacent","subadjacent","unadjacent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjacent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3f2e67b72b06af9967","definition":"Related to; suggestive of; bordering on.","example":"It would be false to suggest CBD is nothing more than an obsession for reiki-adjacent bicoastal millennials.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively, not-comparable, postpositional","register":"figuratively, not-comparable, postpositional","wordFamily":["adjacency","adjacent angle","adjacently","adjacentness","circumadjacent","coadjacent","comic-adjacent","fetish-adjacent","nonadjacent","subadjacent","unadjacent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjacent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9f5df1f2d8e319cebb","definition":"Something that lies next to something else, especially the side of a right triangle that is neither the hypotenuse nor the opposite.","example":"Again, the key colors have twice the area of the adjacents.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["adjacency","adjacent angle","adjacently","adjacentness","circumadjacent","coadjacent","comic-adjacent","fetish-adjacent","nonadjacent","subadjacent","unadjacent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjacent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e6e72f6bd029d1354e","definition":"Next to; beside.","example":"The house adjacent to the school was demolished.","pos":"prep","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["adjacency","adjacent angle","adjacently","adjacentness","circumadjacent","coadjacent","comic-adjacent","fetish-adjacent","nonadjacent","subadjacent","unadjacent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjacent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fbb457486781723d65","definition":"Related to; suggestive of; bordering on.","example":"While Amazon has increasingly become a one-stop shop for some people, we’re also seeing a large proliferation of online companies looking to connect with users wherever they happen to be spending the most time, whether that’s on a social media platform, or on a site that caters to interests adjacent to the businesses’s own — and most importantly not necessarily on the company’s own web properties.","pos":"prep","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["adjacency","adjacent angle","adjacently","adjacentness","circumadjacent","coadjacent","comic-adjacent","fetish-adjacent","nonadjacent","subadjacent","unadjacent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/adjacent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/əˈd͡ʒeɪ.sənt/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/13/En-au-adjacent.ogg/En-au-adjacent.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["adjacency","adjacent angle","adjacently","adjacentness","circumadjacent","coadjacent","comic-adjacent","fetish-adjacent","nonadjacent","subadjacent","unadjacent"]}